# Repository-root ignores. The substantive rules live in vajra/.gitignore, which is where the
# generated data, model bundles and evidence records are decided on.

# =========================================================================================
# MAIN IS PUBLIC. These paths are deliberately absent from this branch and from its history.
#
# They are working material, not deliverables: the deck's source and figures, the internal
# research notes, the design and fix logs, and the challenge brief itself. They live on `beta`,
# which carries the full history.
#
# The rule exists because the working tree may still hold them after a branch switch, and a
# `git add -A` on this branch would put them back into a public commit. Listing them here makes
# that impossible rather than merely unlikely. Files already tracked on `beta` are unaffected —
# git ignores only untracked paths — so this costs that branch nothing.
#
# The two root-level deliverables that DO belong here are the technical document and the deck
# itself, both intentionally not listed.
# =========================================================================================
DECK.md
FIXES.md
Hackathon.md
Solution-Design.md
research/
figures/
make_charts.py
make_deck.py
.claude/

.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Microsoft Office lock files. Created whenever the deck is open, never wanted in history.
~$*

# Deck and document build scratch.
figures/deck/*.tmp
